# FunHub API Documentation

## Purpose

This document defines how FunHub applications communicate with the backend system.

The API acts as the connection between:

- Customer Application
- Business Application
- Admin Dashboard
- Backend Services
- Database

---

# API Technology

Backend Framework:

NestJS

Programming Language:

TypeScript

Communication Format:

REST API

Data Format:

JSON

---

# Authentication

FunHub uses secure authentication.

Methods:

- Email login
- Phone login
- Password authentication
- JWT access tokens
- Refresh tokens

---

# API Structure

Base URL:

/api/v1

Example:

GET /api/v1/businesses

---

# User APIs

## Register User

POST

/users/register

Purpose:

Creates a new customer account.

---

## Login User

POST

/users/login

Purpose:

Authenticates a user.

---

## Get Profile

GET

/users/profile

Purpose:

Returns user information.

---

# Business APIs

## Register Business

POST

/businesses/register

Purpose:

Allows businesses to join FunHub.

---

## View Businesses

GET

/businesses

Purpose:

Returns entertainment businesses.

Filters:

- Location
- Category
- Rating
- Price
- Availability

---

## Business Details

GET

/businesses/{id}

Purpose:

Returns complete business information.

---

# Booking APIs

## Create Booking

POST

/bookings

Purpose:

Allows customers to reserve experiences.

---

## View Bookings

GET

/bookings

Purpose:

Shows customer booking history.

---

# Review APIs

## Create Review

POST

/reviews

Purpose:

Allows customers to share experiences.

---

## View Reviews

GET

/reviews/{businessId}

Purpose:

Shows customer feedback.

---

# Payment APIs

## Create Payment

POST

/payments

Purpose:

Processes transactions.

---

## Payment Status

GET

/payments/{id}

Purpose:

Checks payment status.

---

# Search APIs

## Nearby Search

GET

/search/nearby

Purpose:

Finds entertainment places close to customers.

Filters:

- Distance
- Category
- Rating
- Offers
- Customer experience

---

# Notification APIs

Handles:

- Booking updates
- Promotions
- Messages
- System notifications

---

# Security Rules

All APIs must implement:

- Authentication checks
- Permission checks
- Input validation
- Rate limiting
- Error handling
- Activity logging

---

# Future API Expansion

The API should support:

- Hotel booking
- Flight booking
- Transportation
- AI recommendations
- Event planning

---

# Engineering Principle

The API must be:

- Secure
- Reliable
- Fast
- Easy to expand
